From e14e6482e6028ee1a1f20c3b5b5de53baef55cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 142/202] drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: Start in command mode at power
 on

The DSI is only switched to video mode once the bridge is enabled, so
power-on assumes command mode, but the engine reset does not clear
DSI_MODE_CTRL. On MT6858 the bootloader hands over DSI0 in video mode,
so the panel's init commands, sent before the bridge enable, found the
DSI in video mode and waited for a video-frame-done that never came
("Wait DSI IRQ(0x00000008) Timeout", "failed to switch cmd mode"), and
every command failed with -ETIME. Select command mode after the reset.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index 8a9142824..c6ce0e274 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -832,6 +832,8 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 		       dsi->regs + dsi->driver_data->reg_shadow_dbg_off);
 
 	mtk_dsi_reset_engine(dsi);
+	/* The bootloader may hand over a DSI running in video mode */
+	mtk_dsi_set_cmd_mode(dsi);
 	mtk_dsi_phy_timconfig(dsi);
 
 	mtk_dsi_ps_control(dsi, true);
-- 
